From: Andrey Stoyan <andrey.stoyan.csam@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 16:16:15 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 17/43] test(chexc): review-fix coverage -- order, Handler
 wording, incremental both directions, cross-package and generic performs

performs_order_neg (red-first: wrong clause order compiled clean),
incr_performs (red-first: clause-only change invisible to incremental
rebuilds -- caught a hole one layer deeper than the finding that prompted
it, see compiler commit), incr_caps2 (throws twin of the callee-changed
direction), performs_xpkg{,_neg} and performs_generic{,_neg} (coverage gaps
from the code review, green on arrival), plus the Handler<> wording pin in
performs_neg.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
